Third-party components
----------------------

The pipeline depends on, but does not include, the following.
Each carries its own licence:

  Detectron2   Apache-2.0   https://github.com/facebookresearch/detectron2
  PyTorch      BSD-3-Clause https://pytorch.org
  OpenCV       Apache-2.0   https://opencv.org
  LabelMe      GPL-3.0      https://github.com/wkentaro/labelme
  SAM 3        SAM License  https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3

None of them is distributed with this software. Detectron2 and SAM 3 are
both optional and are installed separately by whoever runs the GPU stages.

The SAM 3 licence deserves a note. It is Meta's own "SAM License", not an
OSI-approved licence, and it governs both the sam3 package and the sam3.pt
weights. Its terms, including its acceptable use policy, are neither
granted nor restricted by this project's GPL-3.0, and anyone using the
SAM 3 route should read it. The ultralytics package can load the same
weights and was not used, because it is AGPL-3.0.

See CITATION.cff and README.md for the papers to cite.


Acknowledgement
---------------

The SAM 3 route began as an independent implementation by Talha
(github.com/laiquet) in idtrackerai-enhanced, which integrates SAM 3 and
Detectron2 into idtracker.ai by a different route: running the models
in-process during tracking rather than exporting contours beforehand. No
code was copied. What was taken is the approach -- segmenting from a text
prompt, and falling back on threshold-derived points to recover animals a
text prompt misses -- and the demonstration that it was worth doing at all.
